course: dictionary
lesson: 15650
title: Thereafter: from then on
level: primary-4
stars: 0
explain: Thereafter means after that time, or from then on. It points back to a moment you have just read about. «The bell rang at noon. Thereafter, the children went to lunch.» The bell is the starting point, and thereafter means every time after it.
explain: Thereafter is a formal word, so you will see it in stories, rules and official writing. In everyday speech, people say «after that» instead. In most sentences you can swap the two, and the meaning stays the same.
explain: In maths, thereafter often marks a change. «The pen costs 5 dollars for the first month and 3 dollars each month thereafter.» The first month is different, and the price changes after it.
fact: Thereafter means after that time, or from then on.
fact: «Thereafter» is a formal word; «after that» is the everyday version.
fact: The word «thereafter» always points back to a time or event you have just read about.
fact: «They married and lived happily thereafter.» means they were happy from then on.
fact: In maths, «thereafter» often shows a rule that starts after a first step, such as a new price.
exercise: «The school gate closed at four o'clock. Thereafter, no one could come in.» What does thereafter mean here? | Only once, a long time ago | Very quickly | *After that time, from then on | Before four o'clock
exercise: Which everyday words could replace thereafter in «They lived happily thereafter»? | Instead | *After that | Never | Before that
exercise: «The phone costs 5 dollars for the first month and 3 dollars each month thereafter.» In which month does the price change to 3 dollars? | Never | *The second month, and every month after that | The fifth month only | The first month only
test: «The rain started at noon, and thereafter the river rose.» What does thereafter mean? | Before noon | Very slowly | *From then on | Only at noon
test: «The club opened in May, and thereafter it met every Friday.» Which words best mean thereafter? | Only once | Before May | *After that time | In the middle of the week
exam: Mia says «thereafter» is just a fancy word for «before». Is she right? | Yes, it means at the same time | *No, it means after that time, from then on | Yes, it means before the event | No, it means somewhere else
